    "setup_id": "05601a00c6bc4954635863826740b7b61d18798ad2f99e32a9fef415a652990f",
    "text": "To solve for the area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) in the trapezoid \\(ABCD\\) where \\(\\overline{AD} \\parallel \\overline{BC}\\), \\(\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{CD}\\), \\(\\overline{AC}\\) bisects \\(\\angle BAD\\), and the area of \\(ABCD\\) is 42, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify Key Properties and Relationships:**\n   - Since \\(\\overline{AD} \\parallel \\overline{BC}\\), \\(ABCD\\) is a trapezoid.\n   - \\(\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{CD}\\) implies \\(\\angle ACD = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\overline{AC}\\) bisects \\(\\angle BAD\\), so \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle CAD\\).\n\n2. **Use the Angle Bisector Theorem:**\n   Let \\(\\angle BAD = 2\\theta\\). Then \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle CAD = \\theta\\).\n\n3. **Determine the Angles:**\n   - Since \\(\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{CD}\\), \\(\\angle ACD = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\angle BAC = \\theta\\) and \\(\\angle CAD = \\theta\\), so \\(\\angle BCA = 90^\\circ - \\theta\\).\n\n4. **Analyze the Trapezoid:**\n   - Since \\(\\overline{AD} \\parallel \\overline{BC}\\), \\(\\angle DAB = \\angle ABC\\) and \\(\\angle ADC = \\angle BCA\\).\n\n5. **Use the Perpendicularity and Angle Bisector:**\n   - Since \\(\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{CD}\\), \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is a right triangle with \\(\\angle ACD = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\overline{AC}\\) bisecting \\(\\angle BAD\\) implies that \\(AC\\) is the angle bisector of \\(\\angle BAC\\).\n\n6. **Area Calculation:**\n   - The area of trapezoid \\(ABCD\\) is given as 42.\n   - Let \\(AD = a\\) and \\(BC = b\\). The height from \\(A\\) to \\(BC\\) is the same as the height from \\(D\\) to \\(BC\\), which is the length of \\(CD\\).\n\n7. **Area of Trapezoid:**\n   \\[\n   [ABCD] = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (a + b) \\times h = 42\n   \\]\n   where \\(h\\) is the height from \\(A\\) to \\(BC\\) and also from \\(D\\) to \\(BC\\).\n\n8. **Area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\):**\n   - The area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) can be calculated using the base \\(CD\\) and height \\(h\\).\n   - Since \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is a right triangle, its area is:\n   \\[\n   [\\triangle ACD] = \\frac{1}{2} \\times CD \\times h\n   \\]\n\n9. **Relate Areas:**\n   - Notice that the height \\(h\\) is the same for both the trapezoid and the triangle.\n   - The area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is half the area of the trapezoid because \\(CD\\) is the height and it splits the trapezoid into two equal areas.\n\n10. **Final Calculation:**\n    \\[\n    [\\triangle ACD] = \\frac{1}{2} \\times [ABCD] = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 42 = 21\n    \\]\n\nThus, the area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is \\(\\boxed{21}\\).",
